  "strongest_angle": "Guinness World Records verified Arica’s 0.76 mm average yearly rainfall using long‑term airport data, highlighted the 172‑month rainless stretch from October 1903 to January 1918, and explained how the Atacama Desert’s fog‑driven climate creates the world’s driest inhabited city, affecting residents and tourism.",
